# Public declarations for the two Samsung /system daemons that vendor policy
# needs to name.
#
# Types declared in plat_private are invisible to vendor policy, and these two
# have to be reachable from both sides:
#
#   multiclientd  multiplexes RIL clients, so rild calls into it and it calls
#                 back - 14 denials of "rild -> multiclientd : binder { call }".
#                 rild is a vendor domain, multiclientd is coredomain because
#                 its binary sits on /system, so neither side could express the
#                 rule while the type was private.
#   smdexe        opens /dev/at_mdm0, typed at_device by qcom vendor policy.
#
# Only the domain types live here. Their exec types and their plat-side rules
# stay in sepolicy/private/samsung_system_daemons.te, since nothing in vendor
# policy needs to see those.
type multiclientd, domain, coredomain;
type smdexe, domain, coredomain;
